# fixedbugs, defect 022, panel 122, 2026-09-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: accepted, and sound only by an accident of the emitter — the owner
# slot happens to live past the binding. Panel 122 measured what that slot
# actually promises: one per expression SITE, released at function exit **or
# when its site re-executes, whichever comes first**. In a loop the emitted C
# frees the previous iteration's bytes while the binding still names them.
#
# CAUSE: nothing tied the lend to the call it was lent for. `spec:253` says
# `.cstr()` lends a `str` to C to read for that call, and a binding is not a
# call.
#
# FIX: panel 122 R2. A lend may stand only as an argument of a call. This
# refuses a program that is sound today, deliberately: what makes it sound is
# invisible at the line, and the alternative is a rule resting on when an
# ownership pass releases a slot — a premise about the world, which
# `.claude/rules/module-shape.md` says expires in silence. It is already dead
# inside a loop.

extern "string.h"
    function strlen(s: cstr) -> u64

function measured(s: str) -> u64
    c = s.cstr()  #~ cstr_escapes
    return strlen(s: c)

function main()
    print(measured(s: "abc").to_str())

# Since 2026-09-10 the specification's sections are numbered and a citation names
# the section, never a line (CL-037). The line numbers above were written against
# the layout at commit 834d804f; read today they are:
#   spec:253 is spec § 13 FFI` says
